From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:50:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/35] H14: charge hayro-jbig2's declared-size allocations to
 a per-decode budget

JBIG2 sizes most of its buffers from values the file declares, not from
the data: a bitmap of up to 65535 x 65535 pixels from a few header bytes,
a gray-scale plane of four bytes per grid cell, one copy of a symbol per
export, a symbol-ID context table of 2^SBSYMCODELEN entries. Each is
bounded on its own; nothing bounds their sum, so a stream of a few
hundred bytes can ask for hundreds of gigabytes (a symbol exported
65,535 times through a dictionary that names another 65,535 times).

DecoderContext gains memory_budget (default None, unlimited).
Image::decode_with installs a MemoryBudget for the call, passed by
reference to every site that allocates in proportion to a declared
value; each charges its bytes before allocating them, and a charge that
would exceed the budget fails the decode with the new
OverflowError::MemoryBudget. Charges are cumulative over the call and
never refunded. Image::decode stays unbudgeted.

Counted: every Bitmap (page, generic, refinement, text and halftone
regions, symbols, height-class collectives, aggregations, pattern
collectives and patterns, stored intermediate regions); Bitmap's
derived Clone is replaced by clone_within, and symbol export decodes
its flags first and checks the copies' total before making the first;
the gray-scale value plane and its two bit planes (checked together);
the HSKIP bitmap; the shifted-pattern table; the symbol-ID context
table; uniform and symbol-ID Huffman tables; the symbol, width, pattern
and export lists; the symbol and table lists built from referred-to
segments, whose length is computed and charged before they are built.
Not counted: fixed-size context tables and allocations linear in the
input.
